    "purpose": "Offline replay corpus for the Academic Connector benchmark (lib/services/__tests__/academic-retrieval-benchmark.test.ts). Sandbox egress to the academic APIs was blocked (TLS handshake reset), so bodies were captured out-of-band from the live APIs on the capture date and stored as compact projections.",
    "providers": {
      "openalex": "GET https://api.openalex.org/works?search=<q>&per_page=5&sort=relevance_score:desc&select=id,doi,display_name,publication_year,type,cited_by_count,is_retracted,open_access[,primary_location]",
      "crossref": "GET https://api.crossref.org/works?query=<q>&rows=5&sort=relevance&select=DOI,title,author,issued,container-title,publisher,is-referenced-by-count,URL,type[,update-to]  and  GET https://api.crossref.org/works/<doi>",
      "semanticscholar": "GET https://api.semanticscholar.org/graph/v1/paper/search?query=<q>&limit=5&fields=paperId,title,year,venue,authors,citationCount,influentialCitationCount,openAccessPdf,externalIds,url  and  GET /paper/DOI:<doi>",
      "arxiv": "GET https://export.arxiv.org/api/query?id_list=1706.03762"
    },
    "trimming": [
      "OpenAlex works were fetched with `select=` (no authorships / abstract_inverted_index / referenced_works). `authors` for OpenAlex records were therefore filled from the sibling Semantic Scholar / Crossref record of the same DOI or from public metadata; records whose author list could not be reconstructed keep `authors: []`, which the real parser maps to the `Unknown Author` sentinel (see field `authorsSource`).",
      "OpenAlex `venue` / `publisher` for compact records were filled from the sibling providers / public metadata when `primary_location` was not part of the projection (field `venueSource`).",
      "Abstracts were not captured (size). Field-completeness for `abstract` is therefore NOT measured in recorded mode.",
      "The arXiv Atom body is reconstructed from the captured entry values (title, published, updated, summary, authors, comment) because the capture tool renders XML as text.",
      "Semantic Scholar answered HTTP 429 (anonymous shared pool exhausted) for 4 of 7 attempts during capture. Queries for which no 200 body could be captured are stored with `status: 429` — this is the observed live behaviour, not a simulation."
    ],
    "replayRules": [
      "Year filters: OpenAlex has a real recorded response for `quantum machine learning` + from_publication_date:2024-01-01. For Semantic Scholar (`year=`) and Crossref (`filter=from-pub-date`) the replay applies the same year window to the recorded unfiltered list (both APIs filter server-side; the recorded list is the unfiltered superset).",
      "DOI lookups resolve against any recorded record with that DOI (case-insensitive) across all fixtures of the same provider; a DOI with no recorded record answers 404 for that provider.",
      "Search queries are routed by normalized text (lower-case, punctuation stripped, whitespace collapsed); a token-set Jaccard >= 0.8 fallback routes citation-string titles to the same recorded body.",
      "No Tavily bodies: TAVILY_API_KEY is never set in tests, so the connector skips the provider exactly as in production without a key."
    ]
